|* Post-layout sampler_dff, ASSEMBLED: capture timing, output levels and the
|* reset-window / idle / active supply currents of the raw-tap digitizer,
|* from ONE flat `klt extract --parasitics` of the cell's own composed,
|* DRC-clean and klt lvs-clean GDS (layout/sampler_dff/sampler_dff.gds) --
|* real intra-cell interconnect included, not the ideal inter-leaf-cell wires
|* sim/post-layout-sampler-dff/'s own leaf-cell composition
|* (layout/pex/sampler_dff_pex.spice: three separately-extracted leaf cells,
|* wired together by that deck itself) assumes between the three leaf shapes.
|*
|* Purpose. sim/post-layout-ro-ring5-assembled/'s own header makes the same
|* move for the ring: `layout/pex/`'s leaf-cell composition has NO inter-cell
|* interconnect at all (a lower bound, by construction), so once the whole
|* cell exists as one composed, DRC/LVS-clean GDS, extracting THAT GDS
|* directly -- rather than the leaf cells wired by ideal testbench nets --
|* includes the real wiring between the leaf cells for the first time.
|* spec/decision-records/DR-0007-*.md names this exact re-run in its own
|* "Follow-up required" list: "Once layout/sampler_dff/'s m/mb nets are
|* routed and its klt lvs matches, extract that GDS flat -- the sampler's
|* equivalent of layout/pex-ring/ -- and re-run [this] deck[]. Findings 1
|* and 3 will move; DR-0006's array-scale result suggests roughly another
|* 1.5x - 1.7x on top of intra-cell alone." Both nets are now routed (mb:
|* PR #95; m: PR #99) and layout/sampler_dff/'s own klt lvs is a full match
|* (22/22 devices, 14/14 nets, 0 mismatches) -- see
|* layout/sampler_dff/README.md and layout/pex-sampler-dff-assembled/README.md.
|*
|* This deck re-runs ONLY the capture-timing/reset-contention deck
|* (sim/post-layout-sampler-dff/tb_post_layout_sampler_dff.spice's own
|* scope), not its sibling setup-time-bracket deck
|* (tb_post_layout_sampler_setup.spice) -- matching
|* sim/post-layout-ro-ring5-assembled/'s own precedent of adding one deck per
|* "assembled" increment rather than replaying every existing deck at the new
|* extraction scope. The setup-time-bracket re-run (DR-0007 finding 3) is
|* left as follow-up.
|*
|* Why a same-deck comparison against the PRE-LAYOUT cell, not against the
|* leaf-cell composition. Same argument sim/post-layout-ro-ring5-assembled/'s
|* own header makes: the two campaigns are two separate extractions (this
|* one, plus layout/pex/sampler_dff_pex.spice), so a ratio between them
|* would not be a same-deck ratio in the sense every other ratio in this repo
|* is. A reader wanting "how much did the real inter-leaf-cell wiring cost
|* beyond the ideal-wire leaf composition" compares THIS record's own
|* pex-vs-pre ratio against sim/post-layout-sampler-dff/'s own matching
|* (temp, Vdd, corner) record directly -- both grids are identical.
|*
|* Topology, stimulus, waveform and PVT grid are otherwise UNCHANGED from
|* sim/post-layout-sampler-dff/tb_post_layout_sampler_dff.spice -- see that
|* file's own header for the full narrative (the reset-contention condition,
|* the four-(temp, Vdd)-point grid, the substrate-tie rationale). The only
|* difference is which post-layout library and subcircuit name the deck
|* instantiates: `sampler_dff_assembled_pex` (this cell's own composed
|* assembly, one flat-extracted circuit) in place of `sampler_dff_pex` (a
|* wrapper hand-assembling three separately-extracted leaf cells with ideal
|* wires), and `ro_buf_pex` (layout/pex-sampler-dff-assembled/pex.json's own
|* self-contained copy of the inverter, same GDS as
|* layout/pex/pex-sampler.json's `sampler_inv_pex`) as the post-layout output
|* load in place of `sampler_inv_pex`.
|*
|* This file is a TEMPLATE: sim/bin/corner-run.py substitutes /home/ubuntu/.volare/volare/sky130/versions/c6d73a35f524070e85faff4a6a9eef49553ebc2b/sky130A/libs.tech/combined/sky130.lib.spice,
|* ss, /home/ubuntu/GitHub/sky130-trng/.loom/worktrees/issue-22/design/sampler_core.spice (pointed at design/sampler_core.spice, as in the
|* sibling deck), /home/ubuntu/GitHub/sky130-trng/.loom/worktrees/issue-22/layout/pex-sampler-dff-assembled/sampler_dff_assembled_pex.spice (pointed at
|* layout/pex-sampler-dff-assembled/sampler_dff_assembled_pex.spice),
|* 27.0, 1.8 and 5p. As committed it is not a runnable deck.
|
|.option scale=1u
|.lib "/home/ubuntu/.volare/volare/sky130/versions/c6d73a35f524070e85faff4a6a9eef49553ebc2b/sky130A/libs.tech/combined/sky130.lib.spice" ss
|
|* pre-layout subcircuit library -- design/sampler_core.spice, which carries
|* both the flat `.subckt sampler_dff` under test and the `.subckt ro_buf`
|* used as its output load on the pre-layout side.
|.include "/home/ubuntu/GitHub/sky130-trng/.loom/worktrees/issue-22/design/sampler_core.spice"
|* post-layout ASSEMBLED subcircuit library (sampler_dff_assembled_pex +
|* its own ro_buf_pex), generated from layout/sampler_dff/'s composed GDS
|.include "/home/ubuntu/GitHub/sky130-trng/.loom/worktrees/issue-22/layout/pex-sampler-dff-assembled/sampler_dff_assembled_pex.spice"
|
|.temp 27.0
|
|* --- substrate return node: hard tie (see header) ----------------------
|Vsub vsubs 0 dc 0
|
|* --- shared stimulus, identical for both sides -------------------------
|* clk: low through reset and idle, then two rising edges at 50 ns and 80 ns.
|Vclk clk 0 PWL(0 0  50n 0  50.1n 1.8  60n 1.8  60.1n 0
|+ 80n 0  80.1n 1.8  90n 1.8  90.1n 0)
|* rst_n: asserted (low) for the first 25 ns, released thereafter.
|Vrstn rst_n 0 PWL(0 0  25n 0  25.1n 1.8)
|* d: high across reset (the contention condition -- see header), falling at
|* 70 ns while the master is transparent so the second edge captures a 0.
|Vd d 0 PWL(0 1.8  70n 1.8  70.1n 0)
|
|* --- the two DFFs under test, one supply source each --------------------
|Vddp vddp 0 dc 1.8
|xdp d clk rst_n qp vddp 0 sampler_dff_assembled_pex
|Vddq vddq 0 dc 1.8
|xdq d clk rst_n qq vddq 0 sampler_dff
|
|* --- output load: one inverter per side, on its own supply --------------
|* design/sampler_core.spice taps q into the digital section; loading both
|* sides identically (post-layout inverter on the post-layout DFF,
|* pre-layout inverter on the pre-layout DFF) keeps the comparison fair
|* without letting the load's own current contaminate either DFF's supply.
|Vddl vddl 0 dc 1.8
|xlp qp qpb vddl 0 ro_buf_pex
|xlq qq qqb vddl 0 ro_buf
|
|.tran 5p 100n
|
|.control
|run
|
|* --- capture timing: clk -> q, both directions -------------------------
|* First clk rising edge (50 ns) captures d = 1; second (80 ns) captures
|* d = 0. Measured at the 50% crossing on both signals.
|meas tran tcq_rise_pex TRIG v(clk) VAL='0.5*1.8' RISE=1
|+ TARG v(qp) VAL='0.5*1.8' RISE=1
|meas tran tcq_rise_pre TRIG v(clk) VAL='0.5*1.8' RISE=1
|+ TARG v(qq) VAL='0.5*1.8' RISE=1
|meas tran tcq_fall_pex TRIG v(clk) VAL='0.5*1.8' RISE=2
|+ TARG v(qp) VAL='0.5*1.8' FALL=1
|meas tran tcq_fall_pre TRIG v(clk) VAL='0.5*1.8' RISE=2
|+ TARG v(qq) VAL='0.5*1.8' FALL=1
|
|* The headline ratios: same cell, same corner, same stimulus, parasitics
|* on vs. off.
|let slowdown_tcq_rise = tcq_rise_pex / tcq_rise_pre
|let slowdown_tcq_fall = tcq_fall_pex / tcq_fall_pre
|
|* --- captured levels: is the post-layout cell functionally correct? -----
|* After the 50 ns edge q must be a solid 1 and hold it through the 70 ns
|* d transition (the slave is opaque then); after the 80 ns edge a solid 0.
|* Worst case within each hold window, so a droop or a glitch shows up.
|meas tran vq_hi_pex MIN v(qp) from=55n to=79n
|meas tran vq_hi_pre MIN v(qq) from=55n to=79n
|meas tran vq_lo_pex MAX v(qp) from=85n to=100n
|meas tran vq_lo_pre MAX v(qq) from=85n to=100n
|let vq_hi_frac_pex = vq_hi_pex / 1.8
|let vq_hi_frac_pre = vq_hi_pre / 1.8
|let vq_lo_frac_pex = vq_lo_pex / 1.8
|let vq_lo_frac_pre = vq_lo_pre / 1.8
|
|* Reset must hold q at 0 while d drives the opposite value.
|meas tran vq_rst_pex MAX v(qp) from=15n to=25n
|meas tran vq_rst_pre MAX v(qq) from=15n to=25n
|
|* --- supply current: reset window, idle, active ------------------------
|* i(Vsrc) is negative for current delivered by the source, so every printed
|* figure is sign-flipped to read as consumed current.
|* i_rst_*  : DR-0014's contention measurement, re-derived for sky130 on
|*            this repo's own storage-loop topology (see
|*            sim/post-layout-sampler-dff/'s own header), now at the
|*            ASSEMBLED extraction scope.
|* i_idle_* : quiescent current with the clock stopped low, reset released.
|* i_act_*  : average over the whole two-edge capture sequence.
|meas tran irstp AVG i(Vddp) from=15n to=25n
|meas tran irstq AVG i(Vddq) from=15n to=25n
|meas tran iidlp AVG i(Vddp) from=35n to=45n
|meas tran iidlq AVG i(Vddq) from=35n to=45n
|meas tran iactp AVG i(Vddp) from=45n to=100n
|meas tran iactq AVG i(Vddq) from=45n to=100n
|let i_rst_pex = -irstp
|let i_rst_pre = -irstq
|let i_idle_pex = -iidlp
|let i_idle_pre = -iidlq
|let i_act_pex = -iactp
|let i_act_pre = -iactq
|
|print tcq_rise_pex
|print tcq_rise_pre
|print tcq_fall_pex
|print tcq_fall_pre
|print slowdown_tcq_rise
|print slowdown_tcq_fall
|print vq_hi_frac_pex
|print vq_hi_frac_pre
|print vq_lo_frac_pex
|print vq_lo_frac_pre
|print vq_rst_pex
|print vq_rst_pre
|print i_rst_pex
|print i_rst_pre
|print i_idle_pex
|print i_idle_pre
|print i_act_pex
|print i_act_pre
|.endc
|.end
|

